  "finding": "The explicit Java experiment confirms 23/30 returned frames on the exposed camera recording, versus 0/30 with edition 152. It has 31/42 correct visible/partial observations, 11 withheld, 0 wrong overlaps, 0/30 hidden outputs and 0 matches to the labelled red object. Both new rendered return cases recover correct observations; wrong-only, changed-quadrant and identical-copy returns are refused. The paired search measurement is 4.35× faster with exactly identical scalar/optimized traces. Defaults remain unchanged; this is recorded evidence, not fresh physical validation.",
